NBalance.mcc/NBalance.mcc

    NAME
        NBalance.mcc -- Resize adjacent groups with pointer feedback.

    SUPERCLASS
        Balance.mui

    DESCRIPTION
        Inherit balancing behavior from Balance and add pointer feedback plus
        neighbouring-weight import/export. This source defines version 15.19.
        Use a balance object between two live siblings in a parent group.
        Setup records the parent group type and registers mouse
        movement/button handling. AROS creates horizontal and vertical
        pointerclass objects. Individual pointer allocation failures do not
        make setup fail. The window pointer is reset to default when hidden by
        this class; a previous custom pointer is not saved.
        To participate in application preference saving, assign a nonzero
        unique ObjectID. Export stores the immediately preceding/following
        sibling weights under that ID as two native ULONG values, choosing
        horizontal or vertical weights from Group_Horiz. Import applies only
        positive saved values. The class itself does not write a preferences
        file.
        Both-zero export leaves an existing dataspace entry untouched. Import
        does not restore zero weights, validate the item length, or convert
        byte order. Both methods return zero and do not propagate dataspace
        failure. Keep the sibling layout and data representation compatible.
        FindNeighbours reports success when a following child exists even if
        there is no predecessor. Supply both neighbours. The pointer cleanup
        path disposes its objects without explicitly resetting the window
        pointer first; do not infer a complete pointer-lifetime guarantee from
        Cleanup alone.

