NBalance.mcc/MUIA_NBalance_Pointer

    NAME
        MUIA_NBalance_Pointer -- Enable resize-pointer feedback.

    INPUTS
        Initialize/set/get; LONG. Off (0) disables event-driven feedback;
        Standard (1) is the default.

    FUNCTION
        Any nonzero stored value takes the same enabled event path; it is not
        a custom pointer-object address. Direction comes from the parent group
        type captured at setup. Pointer display is skipped while the window
        sleeps.
        Setting Off immediately resets the custom pointer only when
        mouseSelectDown is TRUE. A pointer shown merely by hovering is not
        unconditionally reset by this setter; subsequent disabled events do
        not run the pointer logic. Do not assume immediate reset in every
        state.
        Set replaces the own tag with TAG_IGNORE before superclass dispatch,
        so ordinary superclass attribute notification is not generated for it
        by this path. Get returns the stored mode. Provide writable tags. This
        attribute controls feedback, not superclass resizing or persistence.

